 "title": "The Home-Grown Table",
 "theme": "Home-grown food, where food comes from and not wasting it",
 "blurb": "Can goes to the market for the Home-Grown Food table and wants to buy everything; one question from Elif gets him counting on his fingers, and he buys five Amasya apples for five people. At the table, when the milk, eggs, honey and apples find their “homes”, Can takes care of every drop and every bite.",
 "voiceNames": {
  "elif": "Elif",
  "can": "Can",
  "ogretmen": "Miss Nur",
  "pazarci": "The market lady"
 },
 "pages": [
  {
   "text": "On a winter morning, the market was buzzing. “Bright red Amasya apples!” called the market lady. Elif, Can and Miss Nur were there too. Can held the class money box tight. Tomorrow at school they would lay the Home-Grown Food table. Everything on it would come from our own land.",
   "hits": {
    "elif": {
     "say": "My basket's ready, right here in my arms!"
    },
    "can": {
     "say": "Our money box goes jingle jingle!"
    },
    "ogretmen": {
     "say": "Good morning! Have a good day at the stall!"
    },
    "tezgah": {
     "say": "Amasya apples, Finike oranges!"
    },
    "kabak": {
     "say": "Big round pumpkins!"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch the stall!",
   "ask": "Have you ever been to a market? What did you see and hear there?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Can ran to the stall. “Apples, pomegranates, tangerines… Let's buy them all!” Elif smiled. “How many of us will be at the table?” Can counted on his fingers: “Me, you, Miss Nur, Zeynep, Deniz… Five!” Then he beamed: “So, five apples!” The money box jingled.",
   "mech": {
    "done": "Five apples, five people! The rest goes back in the box: jingle!",
    "msg": "Five apples in the basket!"
   },
   "hits": {
    "can": {
     "say": "I paid, and the change goes in the box!"
    },
    "elif": {
     "say": "How many of us will be at the table?"
    },
    "pazarci": {
     "say": "Five apples, here you are! Enjoy!"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Count, and put them in the basket!",
   "ask": "Can wanted to buy everything. What do you want when you go shopping? Which things do you really need?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Next morning, the table was laid in class. The apples came from the market. The milk, eggs and honey from home. Can lifted the milk bottle. “This milk came from the fridge!” Elif giggled. “And how did it get into the fridge?” Can thought and thought… Hmm!",
   "hits": {
    "can": {
     "say": "This milk came from the fridge!"
    },
    "elif": {
     "say": "And how did it get into the fridge?"
    },
    "kar": {
     "say": "Big soft snowflakes are falling!"
    },
    "yum": {
     "say": "Eggs from home."
    },
    "bal": {
     "say": "Sweet-smelling honey from home."
    },
    "elma": {
     "say": "Bright red apples from the market."
    }
   },
   "predict": {
    "q": "Where do you think the milk was before the fridge?",
    "res": "Both are right! Let's go right back to the start.",
    "opts": [
     {
      "l": "In a cow in the barn"
     },
     {
      "l": "At the market"
     }
    ]
   },
   "hint": "Touch Can!",
   "ask": "What's in your fridge at home? Where might those things have come from?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Miss Nur put four pictures on the board: a cow, a hen, a beehive, an apple tree. “Let every food find its home!” Moo! Cluck cluck! Buzz! Rustle rustle! Milk, eggs, honey, apples… Which one came from where?",
   "mech": {
    "done": "Every food found its home!",
    "msg": "They all found their homes!"
   },
   "hits": {
