    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Can looked at the table. For this milk, a cow had eaten hay. A hen had laid the eggs. For the honey, bees had flown flower to flower. A farmer in Amasya had picked the apples. Can held the milk tight: “Not one drop must spill!” Elif added: “One glass each. If it's not enough, we'll pour more!” Glug, glug!",
   "mech": {
    "done": "Five glasses, five friends. Just enough!",
    "msg": "A glass of milk for everyone!"
   },
   "hits": {
    "can": {
     "say": "Not one drop must spill!"
    },
    "elif": {
     "say": "If it's not enough, we'll pour more!"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Pour milk into the glasses!",
   "ask": "What can we do so that no food is left over at the table?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Chomp chomp, crunch crunch! The glasses were empty, and not one apple was left in the basket. Can giggled. “Good thing we didn't buy everything!” Then he waved at the pictures: “Thank you, cow! Thank you, hen! Thank you, bees! Thank you, farmer!” Five people, five empty glasses, five smiling faces.",
